PATCH 300: reconstruct the cockpit-view BUILD ENTRY chain (5d43 -> 44be -> 466c -> 7751) so the mission
ACCEPT path enters the per-vehicle cockpit-template builder without SIGSEGV.  The recurring DGROUP
near-offset base-loss class: DAT_2000_3ae0 / DAT_2000_2d34 hold the player-vehicle NEAR OFFSET (0xc05c,
DS=DGROUP=0x1c00) but the build fns deref them RAW as host pointers.  Reached (gdb, genuine
BATTLES(160,100)->OK(205,128)->ACCEPT(40,186) AZER1) via 459a -> 5cce -> 5d43 -> 44be -> 466c -> 7740 ->
1cdb -> 1ff5 -> 201a -> 7751; patch 299 unblocked the 2ce7 gate so this chain now runs.  All asm-verified
vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin (DS=DGROUP=0x1c00):

  5d43 (0x5d43): `mov di,[0x7ae0]; cmp [di],3; test [di+0x16],1/8` -> rebase g_mem+0x1c000+off.
  44be (0x44be): `andb 0x17(%di),0xfd; orb 0x1,0x1a(%di)` -> rebase the two di byte derefs.
  466c (0x466c): `mov si,[di]` (vehicle type) + dispatch near[si*2+0x6d7c] (per-vehicle template builder
                 7740/8791) -> rebase *param_1 and the DGROUP method-table read.
  7751 (0x77a1): `mov di,[0x6d34]; movb [di+0x3f],0; movb [di+0xa0],0; orb [di+0x1a],0x20` -> rebase.

MISSION-PATH ONLY (d548/2ce7-gated); the 19 verify flows are menu/pre-mission and never enter 459a's
cockpit build -> behaviour-neutral.

